# End-to-End Fraud-Detection ML Monitoring Stack Troubleshooting

## Overview

Diagnosed and resolved three silent configuration and wiring defects across an end-to-end ML observability pipeline (`Evidently` drift scorer -> `Flask` metric-emitter -> `Prometheus` -> `Grafana`) for a fraud-detection model, then provisioned a tagged Grafana overview dashboard via HTTP API.

---

## Architecture & Pipeline Flow

* **Host Drift Scorer (`drift/drift_scorer.py`):** Evaluates per-feature Population Stability Index (PSI) every 15 seconds into `drift/drift_scores.json` and publishes runs to the Evidently UI (`:8000`).
* **Metric Emitter (`metric-emitter`, `:5000`):** Flask exporter reading `DRIFT_SCORES_PATH` (`/drift/drift_scores.json`) and republishing Evidently drift scores alongside serving signals (`flask_http_request_total`, `prediction_accuracy`, `evidently_drift_share`, `model_inference_duration_seconds`).
* **Prometheus (`mon-prometheus`, `:9090`):** Scrapes `metric-emitter:5000/metrics` every 5 seconds.
* **Grafana (`mon-grafana`, `:3000`):** Connects to the provisioned Prometheus datasource on `:9090` and renders live dashboards (`admin` / `grafana2026`).

---

## Root-Cause Analysis & Fixes

| Layer | Symptom | File | Root Cause | Resolution |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Exporter** | `GET /metrics` returned `404` | `app/metric_emitter.py` | Route decorator was set to `@app.route("/prom-metrics")` instead of `/metrics` | Updated route to `@app.route("/metrics")` and recreated container |
| **Scraper** | `metric-emitter` listed as `DOWN` in Prometheus | `prometheus.yml` | Scrape target pointed to `metric-emitter:8000` instead of port `5000` | Updated target to `metric-emitter:5000` and recreated `mon-prometheus` |
| **Datasource** | Grafana panels empty despite fresh Prometheus samples | `grafana/provisioning/datasources/prometheus.yml` | Provisioned datasource URL pointed to `http://prometheus:9091` instead of `:9090` | Updated URL to `http://prometheus:9090` and recreated `mon-grafana` |

